{"term":"appropriate","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:85727ca389df23f2ac","definition":"To take to oneself; to claim or use, especially as by an exclusive right.","example":"Let no man appropriate the use of a common benefit.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["help oneself"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["appropriater","appropriative","appropriator","disappropriate","malappropriate","misappropriate","reappropriate","unappropriate"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/appropriate#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:ffc42cf94523f449cd","definition":"To set apart for, or assign to, a particular person or use, especially in exclusion of all others; with to or for.","example":"A spot of ground is appropriated for a garden.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["allocate"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["appropriater","appropriative","appropriator","disappropriate","malappropriate","misappropriate","reappropriate","unappropriate"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/appropriate#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:fa872e43aa6a8288a1","definition":"To annex (for example a benefice, to a spiritual corporation, as its property).","example":"Some [benefices] were appropriated to secular ecclesiastical corporations","pos":"verb","synonyms":["impropriate","steal","earmark"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"UK","register":"UK, transitive","wordFamily":["appropriater","appropriative","appropriator","disappropriate","malappropriate","misappropriate","reappropriate","unappropriate"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/appropriate#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:98d911f40af595f1d4","definition":"To make suitable to; to suit.","example":"Under the towers were a number of gloomy subterraneous apartments with vaulted roofs, the use of which imagination was left to guess, and could only appropriate to punishment and horror.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["impropriate","steal","earmark"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"archaic","register":"archaic, transitive","wordFamily":["appropriater","appropriative","appropriator","disappropriate","malappropriate","misappropriate","reappropriate","unappropriate"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/appropriate#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:bfea2ada28baa666bc","definition":"Suitable or fit; proper; felicitous.","example":"The headmaster wondered what an appropriate measure would be to make the pupil behave better.","pos":"adj","synonyms":["felicitous","fitting","suitable"],"antonyms":["inappropriate","unhappy"],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["appropriater","appropriative","appropriator","disappropriate","malappropriate","misappropriate","reappropriate","unappropriate","appropes","appropriately","appropriateness","nonappropriate"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/appropriate#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:f377a18a5e393a53db","definition":"Suitable to the social situation or to social respect or social discreetness; socially correct; socially discreet; well-mannered; proper.","example":"I don't think it was appropriate for the cashier to tell me out loud in front of all those people at the checkout that my hairpiece looked like it was falling out of place.","pos":"adj","synonyms":["felicitous","fitting","suitable"],"antonyms":["inappropriate","unhappy"],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["appropriater","app